# System Architecture Diagram

The current repository implements CoursePulse AI as a TypeScript/pnpm monorepo with a React frontend, Express API, PostgreSQL database, Drizzle ORM schema, server-side classifier, and optional AI-powered syllabus parsing.

## Architecture flow

```text
Student / Faculty Browser
        |
        v
React + Vite frontend
artifacts/coursepulse
        |
        v
Express API server
artifacts/api-server
        |
        +--> Reflection route -> rule-based classifier -> classified_signals table
        |
        +--> Faculty route -> aggregation/reporting -> dashboard outputs
        |
        +--> Course context route -> weekly topics and learning objectives
        |
        +--> Syllabus route -> Mammoth text extraction + Anthropic parser
        |
        v
PostgreSQL database via Drizzle ORM
lib/db/src/schema
```

## Main layers

| Layer | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Presentation | React/Vite, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Recharts |
| API | Express 5 route handlers |
| Classification | `artifacts/api-server/src/lib/classifier.ts` |
| Persistence | PostgreSQL tables defined in `lib/db/src/schema/` |
| API contract | OpenAPI in `lib/api-spec/openapi.yaml` and generated clients |
| Demo data | `scripts/src/seed.ts` and CSV samples in `data/` |
| Governance | `/governance` page, dashboard banners, aggregate-only reporting |

See `docs/architecture_diagram.png` for a visual version.
